  cuerpo: {"prompt":"Create ONE complete 30-second 9:16 cinematic commercial. SILENT VIDEO: AUDIO IS DISABLED. Three physically distinct cameras cover the ENTIRE film, including search, results, chat and typography. Strong aerial depth, close passes, deliberate cuts and dramatic scale. Follow the complete sequence below, never omit the user chat turn.\n\n@Video1 is ONLY the camera-movement reference for the UI: the side-on travelling macro and aerial oblique orbit are essential. Transfer those dimensional camera moves into this new film. The white panels must feel enormous in a real cloud world, with sunlight glinting along beveled edges, foreground mist passing close to lens and clouds reflecting on their sides. Camera motion changes perspective substantially, not merely tilting the horizon. Panels remain fixed in world space while the camera moves around them. Text may be oblique during movement; settle near frontal for reading. Preserve Poppins from the image references, never the condensed type seen in the video reference.\n\nREFERENCE MAP: @Image1 dawn sky; @Image2 empty search; @Image3 completed search; @Image4 results; @Image5 USER TURN ALONE; @Image6 user plus ANSWER with attached purple SKY citation; @Image7 chip glow. @Image8 aircraft approaching; @Image9 underside passage; @Image10 REAR departure AFTER passage (tail toward viewer, nose away). @Image11–@Image14 official views of ONE A320neo, authority for its geometry and paint. @Image15–@Image18 announcement text designs. @Image19 BLUE closing; @Image20 PURPLE closing. @Image21–@Image25 isolated exact text artwork; @Image26–@Image27 official logos. @Image28 UI SIDE MACRO; @Image29 low oblique RESULTS; @Image30 oblique agency type. Camera pose references are keyframes, not static slides.\n\nTHREE CAMERA RIGS: A aerial wide with assertive forward travel; B close lateral slider, later rear chase; C low oblique orbit, later overhead pass. Hard cuts in action, keep one sun at left and one coherent world. Real dawn cloud sea, cobalt sky, warm side/backlight, atmospheric depth. UI and texts have spatial depth; clouds near camera move much faster than distant clouds.\n\n0–2.2s SEARCH, A then B. Begin moving through mist toward the giant empty search field. Type “¿A dónde viajar en Sudamérica?” Immediately cut to B at 0.8s: dramatic side travelling macro as @Image28 and @Video1, skimming along the long rounded edge while last letters finish. Pull clear to see the completed question. Real perspective change, not front-facing zoom.\n2.2–4.2s RESULTS, C. Enter pulse. Three result cards appear one after another below search: Camboriú, Mendoza, Puerto Fuy. Fly past their left edges from a low oblique drone angle like @Image29, then arc to a readable front three-quarter view. Each landing has a subtle lime/purple light pulse. Only search and results exist here.\n4.2–5.6s USER TURN, A. Cards fold away COMPLETELY. The same question reshapes into the right-aligned chat USER BUBBLE @Image5. HOLD THE USER BUBBLE ALONE for one second; no answer and no result cards behind it. This visible beat is mandatory.\n5.6–8.0s LLM RESPONSE, C. A new white answer appears BELOW the existing user bubble and writes “Tres ideas: Camboriú, por sus playas; Mendoza, por sus bodegas; y Puerto Fuy, por sus lagos y volcanes”. A single small purple “SKY Airline” CITATION CHIP appears attached to the end of the answer, exactly @Image6. A gentle lateral camera arc reveals the panel's thickness, then holds the full exchange readable. This is an LLM answer, not another search result.\n8.0–9.5s CITATION, B. Move rapidly from the answer into its purple citation. Purple/lime sparks and restrained rainbow shimmer, then one bright sun-aligned flash. The chip and ALL interface disappear into that flash permanently. No UI or citation after 9.5s.\n9.5–11.8s AIRCRAFT APPROACH, A. One real SKY A320neo emerges from the distant flare already flying toward the lens. Camera is anchored in air, NOT retreating with the plane. Nose points toward viewer with slight screen-right heading. It starts small, then rapidly grows with accelerating perspective until the wings exceed frame width. Atmospheric haze clears as it approaches; nearby cloud wisps rush past. No hovering, no sideways slide. Match @Image8 materials and official geometry.\n11.8–12.7s OVERHEAD PASS, C. Cut on approach to a 24mm camera just below the same flight path. Nose crosses top-right, then huge belly, both engines, wings and finally tail race overhead as @Image9. Brief natural motion blur and pressure shake at closest pass. Aircraft COMPLETELY passes the camera. Constant forward flight, no replay.\n12.7–15.5s DEPARTURE, B. CUT TO REAR THREE-QUARTER @Image10. Camera is now BEHIND the aircraft, looking at its tail cone and engine exhaust exits; nose points AWAY toward upper-right. Plane has ALREADY passed and continuously RECEDES, shrinking into the distance, never returning to a frontal/side approach. Camera advances more slowly than the plane, so separation grows. Clouds stream backward below. Same heading, same daylight, same aircraft, no sudden deceleration. By 15.5s it has left the typography area.\n15.5–18.0s YEAR, A. Moving clean sky. Whole phrase “Un año creando con SKY.” lands in one clean kinetic gesture, fully readable. Aerial camera trucks sideways past nearer cloud layers. No word-by-word retyping.\n18.0–20.5s PROOF, B. Cut closer with a decisive forward move. Keep year above; big lime plus and white “2.000 piezas.” arrive as @Image16. Hold readable. No citation, no plane, no extra graphics.\n20.5–23.0s NEWS, C. Orbit from oblique @Image30 toward frontal @Image17 while the full phrase appears: “Y ahora nos eligió como” / “su agencia SEO/AEO.” Large spatial typography over sky, complete phrase remains for at least two seconds. No chip reappears.\n23.0–25.0s THANKS, A. “¡Gracias, SKY!” as @Image18. Camera cranes upward through cobalt sky; the words remain readable while the sky becomes Efeonce blue.\n25.0–27.0s BLUE LOCKUP. Exact @Image19: Efeonce | SKY in white with efeoncepro.com URL bubble below, on solid BLUE. All elements visible during a two-second hold.\n27.0–28.2s only BACKGROUND changes smoothly BLUE→SKY PURPLE. Marks and URL stay stationary and unchanged.\n28.2–30.0s exact purple @Image20 final hold.\n\nAirplane: official SKY Airbus A320neo only. Real painted aluminum, controlled reflections, cockpit glazing, fine seams, dark fan disks, CFM smooth nacelles, two engines, gear retracted, correct white/purple/lime livery, believable mass. No miniature/plastic CGI finish, no changing fuselage length, no morphing between angles, no contrails, smoke, vapor streams or wing trails. Full flight goes TOWARD camera → OVER camera → AWAY from camera. No repeated approach after the pass. Never put camera names, notes or additional text on screen. Silent output; music and SFX are produced separately.","duration":"30","resolution":"720p","aspect_ratio":"9:16","bitrate_mode":"high","generate_audio":false,"image_urls":["https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba63f/DiU1n69iJAGtd-sUOPWpk_C1-b.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba63f/HnVjmy0EgaswWSm2JxiW__01-search-empty.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba640/KldEJbKEIWNKs3HyjxpMP_02-search-question.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba640/yCxiwl0tjrnnVi1BYDACM_03-results.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba640/R9Y0Dg6lsg8KpbGNy0XZ4_camera-A-user-alone.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba640/u9GozSdS_lwkYxAoRjOof_05-answer-citation.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba641/tTfeYQ-Fg82BFzQLV-wm2_06-chip-glow.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba641/k06KDeF7PJkMvnP2d4ufK_cam-A-frontal-photo.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba641/juWE__oTnvKzY1_F3dQiT_cam-C-overhead-photo.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba641/a6gfarheNO2Nyw9BERcvm_cam-B-rear-departure.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba642/sjFAqAysdiqvqhg5JNUMV_A320neo_CFM_SKY_V02.png","https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaba642/ZvZ34xRTLWU-u7zOzOnos